# Agent-accessible GitHub issues

When asked to implement or select a GitHub issue:

1. Check its labels before making changes.
2. Any issue without the `no-agent` label is open to you; it needs no other label.
3. On a `no-agent` issue you may help, but never be the sole contributor, even when asked: the user must write part of the change themselves. Explain, review, and draft the pieces they ask for; don't implement the whole issue end to end or open its PR on your own.

The `no-agent` label is configured separately in each GitHub repository.
